@* Tooltip's Overview, written by hand after Popover's: placement, icon buttons with shortcuts
   (previewed in each mode). Accessibility (what the trigger needs, what a tooltip can't hold) and
   See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A tooltip is a short hint about a control, shown on hover and on keyboard focus: what an icon does, or its shortcut. For a panel people click to open, with links or a form, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/popover">Popover</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Placement</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Placement</Code> to show the tooltip below, before or after its trigger; it's above by default.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tooltip-sides" />
<TextBlock>With the script, when there's no room on that side, such as above a button at the top of the window, it shows on the opposite side; with JavaScript off it keeps its side.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Icon buttons and shortcuts</Heading>
<TextBlock>Use <Code>Content</Code> for more than plain text, such as a keyboard shortcut in a <Anchor Href="docs/components/kbd">Kbd</Anchor>, and <Code>Delay</Code> for how long a hover waits (300 milliseconds; keyboard focus shows it at once).</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tooltip-icon-buttons" />
<TextBlock>Inside a tooltip, an <Anchor Href="docs/components/icon-button">IconButton</Anchor> leaves out its own <Code>title</Code>, so hovering shows one tooltip, not two; it still needs its <Code>Label</Code>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Tooltip Text="Copy to clipboard">
            <IconButton Icon="Lucide.Copy" Label="Copy" />
        </Tooltip>

        @* Below the trigger, with a shortcut. *@
        <Tooltip Placement="Placement.Bottom">
            <Content>Save <Kbd Keys="Ctrl+S" /></Content>
            <ChildContent><Button>Save</Button></ChildContent>
        </Tooltip>
        """;
}
